    "result_text": "The build passes and all tests are green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133) computed at creation, per the spec.\n\n**New logic** \u2014 `MembershipLevel.of(owner)` starts at 1, adds 1 when an email is present, adds 1 when `namesakeCount` is 0, and caps at 3 (level 4 reserved for tenure):\n- `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/MembershipLevel.java` \u2014 new shared helper so the mapper and the audit line use identical logic.\n\n**Response DTO** \u2014 `membershipTier` removed in favour of `membershipLevel`:\n- `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 replaced the `membershipTier` string schema with a `membershipLevel` integer (int32, min 1, max 3). This regenerates `OwnerDto`.\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 mapping target changed to `membershipLevel` via `expression = \"java(MembershipLevel.of(owner))\"` (dropping the old GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE expression, which was the only thing that consumed `householdMemberCount` for membership).\n\n**Audit line** \u2014 now records the level instead of the tier:\n- `rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 appends `membershipLevel={}` to the create audit line (confirmed in the log: `AUDIT - owner created id=11 ... membershipLevel=3`).\n\n**Stale reference cleanup**:\n- `rest/function/owner/AssignHouseholdSize.java` \u2014 updated the javadoc that claimed `householdMemberCount` drives the GOLD tier; the count is still computed and persisted for reporting but no longer affects membership.\n\nThe `coreNumericLevel` acceptance test (owner with email + unique name \u2192 `membershipLevel == 3`) passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nNote: `householdMemberCount` is still assigned/persisted but is now unused by any response field. I left it in place since removing a persisted column is out of scope for this change \u2014 let me know if you'd like it retired too.",
